WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:05.819
Introversion and extraversion are terms
first coined by psychiatrist Carl Gustav Jung

00:00:05.819 --> 00:00:11.460
in Switzerland in the 1920s
according to Jung an extravert seeks

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:16.800
intensive contact with the outside world
an introvert instead turns the psychic

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:22.289
energy inwards. Jung believed that no one
is a hundred percent extravert or a

00:00:22.289 --> 00:00:26.490
hundred percent introvert instead we
carry both traits

00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:30.810
however most minds tend to lean either
to one side or the other.

00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:35.730
If both characteristics are equally
present we can speak of someone who has

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:44.129
an ambivert personality. In the 1960s the
psychologist Hans Eysenck added to Carl

00:00:44.129 --> 00:00:48.870
Jung's ideas.He argued that the main
difference between introverts and

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:55.230
extraverts lies in the way they gain and
recharge their mental energy. By Nature,

00:00:55.230 --> 00:00:59.850
introverted people have a higher level
of brain activity and therefore feel a

00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:04.489
greater need to shield themselves from
external stimuli. By withdrawing

00:01:04.489 --> 00:01:10.680
themselves they gain mental energy. The
neuronal activity of extraverts is lower.

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:16.470
They overcome this lack by exposing
themselves to external stimulation this

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:23.070
charges their inner batteries. To
illustrate the difference let's compare

00:01:23.070 --> 00:01:29.040
two imaginary children: Jay is
extraverted. He loves to be surrounded by

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:34.049
classmates. He enjoys being the center of
attention and loves to talk to his

00:01:34.049 --> 00:01:38.640
buddies about all kinds of stuff.
He organizes football games with

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:43.500
strangers and right after is open to
playing ping-pong with someone else.

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:50.579
By seeking social stimuli he gains mental
energy. Ann is introverted. As others play

00:01:50.579 --> 00:01:55.829
around in the park, she often enjoys
sitting alone watching. At home, she

00:01:55.829 --> 00:02:01.200
plants herbs in the garden, all by
herself. She slowly becomes a real expert

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:03.893
in this field but that's her secret.

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:10.099
To recharge her batteries Ann needs peace and quiet time.

00:02:10.190 --> 00:02:15.420
Introverts are not necessarily shy, even
if it appears they like to

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:21.150
walk away from small talk. Ann in fact is not shy at all. She is not afraid to talk to anyone,

00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:26.490
not even seniors. When too many people are around and the conversations

00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:32.460
become superficial or confusing she gets
super tired. Her strategy is to fade out

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:38.640
and go inside herself to recharge
through silence. Jay loves to have many

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:44.960
people around him, to jump from one
conversation to the next stimulates him.

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:50.700
Some experts claim that extraverts and
introverts use different brain areas to

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:55.980
form their thoughts. An extravert tends
to use short term memory and therefore

00:02:55.980 --> 00:03:02.070
is able to come to fast associations Jay
therefore talks fast and a lot.

00:03:02.070 --> 00:03:06.000
He appears smart because his brain always offers an answer quickly.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:11.010
However he often speaks before he thinks
and later changes his mind.

00:03:11.010 --> 00:03:16.320
Someone like Ann works with her brain to
carefully retrieve information from her

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:21.480
long-term memory. Her thoughts are more
complex and hence need more time to

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:27.270
develop. She therefore thinks first and
then speaks. If the two were asked for

00:03:27.270 --> 00:03:31.950
directions by a tourist Ann would spend
time thinking about the best answer

00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:37.920
while Jay would have already come up
with different kinds of options.

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:41.730
Good teachers and clever business leaders
know about the different nature of

00:03:41.730 --> 00:03:46.530
introverts and extraverts and try to
develop their strengths. When raising

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:51.440
questions they ask everyone to think for
a minute in silence before answering.

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:55.680
Extraverts then learn to formalize their
thoughts before they speak and

00:03:55.680 --> 00:04:00.420
introverts get more talking time to
practice public speaking.

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:05.490
At brainstorming they use a formal process
or a talking stick to make sure an Ann

00:04:05.490 --> 00:04:08.630
also gets to participate.

00:04:08.989 --> 00:04:14.900
Group projects can be formalized to
support both temperaments. In one project

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:20.579
extraverts and introverts work together.
Jay then learns from Ann how to think

00:04:20.579 --> 00:04:26.190
ideas over to develop more complex
thoughts. Ann in return benefits from

00:04:26.190 --> 00:04:32.250
Jay's fast association skills and learns
to think and speak more flexibly. In the

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:37.020
next project the same temperaments work
together. Then they see their own traits

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:41.310
in the opposite person. If confronted
with problems in teams of the same

00:04:41.310 --> 00:04:46.199
character introverts need to speak up
and extraverts are forced to think deep

00:04:46.199 --> 00:04:51.510
to proceed. The educator Rudolf Steiner
was a proponent of this method for his

00:04:51.510 --> 00:04:58.440
Waldorf schools. Psychologist Jerome
Kagan's research on temperament in

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:02.639
Toddlers showed that many character
traits we are born with make it into

00:05:02.639 --> 00:05:08.669
adulthood. He confronted 500 babies with
different stimuli like loud sounds and

00:05:08.669 --> 00:05:13.800
bad smells. Around 20% of the babies
cried or got nervous,

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:20.130
40% stayed relaxed and the other 40%
were somewhere in between. A second test

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:24.660
years later showed, that babies who
didn't react strongly turned out to be

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:31.979
more extraverted. What about yourself? Do
you consider yourself more introverted

00:05:31.979 --> 00:05:36.900
or extraverted? Or do you think this
classification is flawed and there is no

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:42.229
such thing? Please share your thoughts in
the comments below.

